                <pb facs="0222" n="188" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v07p1/pg188"/>

                <head>No. 77<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi></head>
                <p>On March 21 Ambassador Dunn, Foreign Secretary Eden, and Foreign Minister Schuman
                    considered further the draft reply and agreed on still another draft. This draft
                    was the same in substance as that transmitted in telegram 5749 (see footnote 3,
                        <hi rendition="#italic">supra</hi>) with the exception of the final
                    paragraph which is indicated in footnote 4, <hi rendition="#italic">infra</hi>.
                    This text was transmitted to Washington in a telecon during the morning of March
                    21, and relayed to President Truman the same day with suggested revisions
                    especially in the final paragraph. No copy of the transcript of the telecon has
                    been found in Department of State files; however a message from Secretary
                    Acheson to President Truman, dated March 21, contains the draft text and the
                    suggested revisions. (662.001/3–2152) On March 22 President Truman, who was in
                    Key West, Florida, approved the text of the draft reply subject to the revisions
                    proposed by the Department <pb facs="0223" n="189" xml:id="pg189"/> of State. A
                    telegram containing his approval is attached to the message from Secretary
                    Acheson referred to above.</p>
                <p>For text of the reply as approved by the President, with the two different
                    versions of the final paragraph, see telegram 2209, <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >infra</hi>.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
